  "body": "## Saved data\n- 2026-01-01 to 2026-11-18: 24,291 settled races in 11 month-split public-result CSVs, with venue, real starters, payouts, and source URLs.\n- All 1,068 3-car BOX rows by field size, gender, session and class, with investment, wins, net, ROI, rankings, maximum payout dependence.\n- 10,005 monthly BOX rows across two half-year CSVs, plus source/methodology README, hash manifest, and seven-tested line classifier.\n\n## Validation\n- Historical result source inventory: 24,291 settled races; 62 excluded non-settled or no-payout rows; 0 unsettled-source issues reported in the original bundle.\n- The 17 GitHub data/code/README files were independently fetched after save, and exact normalized Git blob SHA matched on all 17/17.\n- Local line classifier test: 7 passing cases. No claim of GitHub CI success.\n\n## Essential limitation\n- The restored source ZIP does NOT carry independently time-anchored published pre-race lineup snapshots for all 24,291 races. Numbers and rider regions cannot recover original line membership.\n- The classifier distinguishes full same-line three, two of same plus other, and three different lines, solo riders, positions and tied payouts, but nationwide line-frequency statistics remain not formally accepted until lineup sources are joined and independently checked.\n- Do not present this as observed in-race formations or race-video labels. Do not train on unaudited lineup estimates.\n\n## Safety / scope\n- Separate research Draft; do not merge into production without review.\n- Only historical public result derivatives; no private AES forecast plaintext, production key or Secret committed.\n- The original ZIP SHA256 and Library reference are pinned in manifest.\n\n## 2026-11-19 nationwide line-composition acceptance audit\n\nFormal result: **HOLD, not nationwide-finalized**. Across 24,291 settled race-result records, 22,245 men's races are line-composition applicable; 2,046 girls' races are N/A. Of those 22,245, independently source-bound published-lineup originals with verified source bytes/SHA and all-starter alignment available in this PR: **0**. All 22,245 remain UNVERIFIED for line statistics. Prior provisional 64.06%, solo 3,536 and line-of-4 1,006 cannot be reproduced from the archived lineup-less source and must not become official statistics. A source-only fail-closed gate, 8 locally passing tests, machine-readable receipt and explicit missing-data report have been added; exact Git blob readback matched for all four additions. See [acceptance audit](https://github.com/haji84/RACE-AI/blob/research/keirin-box-line-2026-11-19/research/keirin/box_2026_01_01_to_11_18/NATIONWIDE_LINE_AUDIT_20261119.md). No main merge, no predictive model or live scoring changes.\n\n## 2026-11-19: Published-lineup backfill continuation (research)\n\n- Historical public lineup source-linked entries: **6 -> 15**. Added Kokura 1-2R, Ogaki 7-9R and Utsunomiya 1-4R on 2026-11-18; the venue/date/race/actual-starter set and 3-ren-tan were checked against the existing result CSV.\n- Applicable men's race denominator **22,245**; **22,230 remain missing**. Girls 2,046 are N/A. Pilot classifications: same-line three 2, two-from-one-line-plus-other 10, three distinct lines 3. These are not nationwide proportions.\n- Added `published_lineup_more_verified_20261118.jsonl`, `line_matched_15_verified_20261118.csv`, `line_coverage_15_pilot_20261119.json`, `LINE_BACKFILL_PROGRESS_20261119.md`, the bounded `historical_line_backfill.py`, and research-only GitHub Actions workflow `keirin-line-backfill-research.yml`.\n- The workflow is an attempted first batch, **not a verified successful remote collection**. The public source may be unavailable or refuse robots/policy access; do not bypass. Main not touched, real forecast/Secret untouched.\n- Current honest status: PARTIAL, not nationally finalized. Source-bound per-race lines are necessary, but no requirement for pre-cutoff snapshot time attestation or video in this historical publication analysis.\n",
